WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.187 --> 00:00:03.190
- Did you say, "Has it been a hard life?"

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.093
Oh, lord, yeah, it's been a hard life,

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.210
but I don't believe I'd
have it no other way.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.720
- [Mark] All right, Markum Ray.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:15.553
- [Markum] Yeah.

00:00:15.553 --> 00:00:17.460
- [Mark] Markum Ray, where'd you grow up?

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.703
Where are you from originally?

00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:19.860
- [Markum] Right here in Manchester.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.260
- [Mark] And you grew up
with both your parents?

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.443
- Well, yeah.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.480
I grew up one of the poorest kids around.

00:00:28.497 --> 00:00:29.330
- [Mark] One of the poorest?

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:30.540
- Yeah.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.640
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.400
- Well, my childhood, I was stomped,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.280
I was beat by a man that was one of

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.123
the best persons there ever was.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.830
Other than that, it was more mental abuse

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.270
and physical abuse than
you'd know what to do with.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.863
- [Mark] What kind of
stuff you go through?

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.030
- Well, your brains been split
out with everything you can,

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:01.830
stomped in the stomach,
whooped with cords,

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.860
switches and everything else.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.130
- [Mark] This is your dad?

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.300
- Huh?
- This is your dad?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.133
- Yeah.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:13.130
And I've been on my own ever
since I was eight years old.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.340
- Eight years old?
- Yeah.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.823
- [Mark] Why'd you leave at
eight, 'cause it was so rough?

00:01:15.823 --> 00:01:17.450
- Just couldn't stand it no more.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.420
- [Mark] And where'd you go at eight?

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.910
- I went to my grandmother's out here.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:25.110
Stayed with her up 'til I
was about 20 and I left,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.023
then I met a girl named Mary.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.400
Married a girl named Mary
Harris, she was 15 years old.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:36.400
We had two kids and in
1988 we got divorced,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.880
and I still love her more today

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.310
than I did the first day we married.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.288
- [Mark] Did you raise your kids?

00:01:44.288 --> 00:01:49.288
- Well, I went, one of 'em,
her mother and dad raised

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.280
'cause we was too young,
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.340
But we couldn't get a
chance to raise a kid,

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:57.570
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.630
And then our baby boy, I went and got him.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.850
My brother called me one
night and he told me,

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.110
he said, "Ray, if you don't
come and get this kid,"

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.130
said, "I'm gonna take
him to Social Services.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.050
So I went the next day,
got him, brought him home.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:11.241
I laid him down beside my mother.

00:02:11.241 --> 00:02:13.970
He was here up 'til he got

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.940
with another women, with his woman.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.473
- [Mark] What kind of jobs have you had?

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.853
- Tobacco work, roofing.

00:02:26.966 --> 00:02:31.716
Lord, I couldn't tell ya all
what kind of, what I've had.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.253
20-some years on the garbage route.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:41.050
I've owned one home that was stolen

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.653
right out from under me
by a trailer company,

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.832
along with another friend of mine.

00:02:47.832 --> 00:02:50.260
Their trailer was taken
right out from under them,

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.890
it never was even delivered.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.420
They got their money.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.970
And then there was a guy named.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.710
My boy got sick one month

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.010
and I got behind on a trailer payment.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.700
Guy told me, he said, "Ray,"

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.010
he said, "send me a double payment

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.200
first of the month,
everything will be fine."

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.140
I sent a double payment at the
first of the following month.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.530
A week later I was called,

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.230
told me to get out of the trailer.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:22.330
- [Mark] So you grew up here
in Manchester, Kentucky?

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.050
This is, you know, deep
in Appalachia, very poor.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.250
- Right.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.260
- [Mark] It's one of the
poorest parts of Kentucky, even.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.093
- Exactly.

00:03:29.093 --> 00:03:29.926
- [Mark] So that means it's the poorest

00:03:29.926 --> 00:03:31.103
part of the country, probably.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:33.283
What's it like growing up here?

00:03:33.283 --> 00:03:34.200
You love Appalachia?

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.560
- I love Manchester more
than anything in the world.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.313
It's just so hard here,
there's no work to do,

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.610
and I've been in and out of jail

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.570
more times than you
could count for drug use,

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:50.040
but I never was caught with no drugs,

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.173
and things like that.

00:03:52.262 --> 00:03:54.112
There ain't no wonder there's so many

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:58.600
fighting, arguing, stealing
and all this stuff,

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.560
there's no work for people to do.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:01.810
I mean, son, I know some of

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.710
the smartest people there are around,

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.000
smarter than college students.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.450
Like these right down here at
this store right down here,

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.740
some of the best people you'll ever meet.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.740
Some of the smartest people,
they're builders of everything,

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.480
and there's just no work
around here for 'em to do.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.713
- [Mark] Yeah, that's the problem here.

00:04:21.713 --> 00:04:23.480
It's so remote, so rural.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:24.313
- Yeah.

00:04:24.313 --> 00:04:26.210
- [Mark] That there's,
there are no factories,

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.220
there's no jobs here, there's no nothing.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.260
- There ain't nothing here.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:32.160
- [Mark] What kind of
schooling did you get?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.083
- Eighth grade.

00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:34.004
- [Mark] Eighth grade.

00:04:34.004 --> 00:04:36.004
- I dropped out when I was 15 years old.

00:04:37.455 --> 00:04:38.400
- [Mark] But you can read and write?

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.233
- Yeah.

00:04:40.566 --> 00:04:41.399
- [Mark] And what do you do for fun here?

00:04:41.399 --> 00:04:43.470
What do you do for enjoyment?

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.510
- Well, I leave about
the crack of daylight,

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.183
after losing everything I had right there.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:53.090
Almost $34,000 worth of stuff that,

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.820
like most people go to a furniture store

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.560
and pay two or $300 for,

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.980
I had to wind up paying for mine

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.060
by the month, 18, 24 months.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.350
I had almost $34,000 worth of stuff

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.480
ruined right there in that
trailer, plus my home, too.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.910
- [Mark] So that trailer's
empty and now you live in this?

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.130
- Well, no, it ain't empty,

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.970
it's got my things sitting in it,

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.180
but there's so many snakes
crawling around here

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.113
and things that it just,

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:16.300
I killed a copperhead crawling

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.150
right out of that wall the other day.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.570
I stay on the road most of the time.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:26.210
I come here at my mom's, I
lay down and I go to sleep.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.993
I'm back up the next morning,
I'm on the road again.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.117
I built my own bike, I
got a one-of-a-kind bike

00:05:33.117 --> 00:05:35.593
and there ain't another
one on the road like it.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:38.943
- [Mark] Where have you traveled?

00:05:38.943 --> 00:05:40.270
You've been around the country?

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:43.373
- I've been to Detroit, Chicago, Georgia,

00:05:45.891 --> 00:05:47.903
Ohio, Cincinnati, Hamilton.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.960
Ain't too many places around
the Southeast I ain't been.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.813
- [Mark] You ever think about leaving?

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.960
- Well, I've spent three-fourths
of my life on the road,

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.190
and I just grew tired of it.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.890
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:03.130
- Huh?
- How old are you?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.787
- 57.
- 57.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.940
And your health is good?

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.600
- Well, no, my health ain't that good.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.633
I was diagnosed with cancer back about,

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.550
almost five years ago.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:17.460
- [Mark] What kind of cancer?

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.430
- Brain cancer.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:19.263
- [Mark] Brain cancer?

00:06:19.263 --> 00:06:20.096
- Yeah.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.500
You can't get no way around here

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.060
to get nowhere to go
nowhere or do nothing.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:30.630
I was supposed to have went
to a cancer center, didn't go,

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:32.680
so I picked me up a Bible,

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:33.890
and I'm doing things now

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:37.160
that I never done before in my life.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.560
I get out, I go places, things that I

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.293
used to love to do when I was growing up

00:06:42.293 --> 00:06:43.743
that I don't even do anymore,

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.850
and, other than that-

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:48.360
- [Mark] So you didn't do chemotherapy

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.193
or anything like that?

00:06:49.193 --> 00:06:50.026
- No.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.670
- [Mark] How'd you treat it?

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.543
- With the Bible.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.633
With the Bible and these two hands.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.333
I've moved, let's see.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:02.910
With just my cousin down there,
he had a place on his leg

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:04.940
which had moved right here.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:09.940
I moved a place off his chest,
within 30 days it was gone.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.963
Cousin had a blockage
right here, moved that.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:17.810
It's just with these hands.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.320
- [Mark] So drugs were a part
of your life at one point?

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.690
- Lord, yeah, I got hooked
up on, I got on some,

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:28.560
I always had bad headaches all my life,

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:31.060
and one day I was going
through Laurel County

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.590
and I was gonna stop
and get me some Tylenol

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:35.010
and a girl I was with, she said, "Here,"

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.510
she said, "here's something."

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:41.480
Said, "Take it," said, "it'll
take care of your headache."

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:45.470
Well, 30 days later (coughs)

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.400
after taking those two things,

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.247
I felt like I could walk on air.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:53.130
From then on, that was from 1992 on up,

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:56.020
I was on drugs up 'til
about four years ago, bad.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:58.000
Cocaine, pills, drinking,

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.470
which, I always smoked a little pot,

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:02.860
but, other than that, I tried meth twice,

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:03.723
I throwed it down, I said,

00:08:03.723 --> 00:08:05.573
"No, I don't want none of that crap."

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.460
And only one thing I never
did do was get to the needle.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.870
That's the God's honest truth.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.019
- [Mark] So what were
you telling me earlier

00:08:14.019 --> 00:08:16.340
about your family,
something that happened?

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.730
- [Markum] My granddaughter,
back when she was

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:21.423
about three years old, she was
brutally raped by somebody.

00:08:24.181 --> 00:08:27.190
I don't know if they ever
did find out who done it,

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.660
and I said right then and there,

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.880
if I ever found out who
done that baby like that,

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.451
that they never would
do nobody else that way.

00:08:33.451 --> 00:08:34.950
- [Mark] And they never caught the guy?

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.300
- [Markum] I never did
know if they did or not.

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.230
- [Mark] Is there a lot
of crazy behavior here?

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:42.530
- [Markum] Crazy (laughs).

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:46.627
Look at the side of that house right there

00:08:46.627 --> 00:08:48.970
and you'll see what I (laughs).

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.495
See right there, them bullet holes?

00:08:50.495 --> 00:08:51.495
- [Mark] Oh.

00:08:52.443 --> 00:08:54.073
- It's where they mess around.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:59.310
Every now and then you gotta look out,

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.090
see who's around your
house and everything.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:02.553
Most people go to bed with,

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.590
they lock their doors and everything.

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:07.350
I sleep with mine open 'cause they know

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.850
I ain't gonna tolerate their bull crap.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:11.600
I'm telling you God's honest truth.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.900
One day my cousin came up missing,

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.520
and when they found him, he had been,

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:24.387
his throat had been cut, he
had been burnt, been strangled,

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.360
and my cousin, his daughter,
came out here that day

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.780
asking me would I help go find him

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:33.823
and I told her yeah.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.380
My worst fears all my life came true

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:42.583
and we run up on her
dad back in that holler.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.880
And that was the worst fear
I'd ever felt in my life.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:53.040
I mean, it didn't exactly sink
in at the time I seen him.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.220
I walked all the way around him.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:59.550
I didn't get exactly what it
was, you know what I'm saying?

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:03.020
But when it did dawn on me,
I started doing pain pills,

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:05.447
and when I did it, I was running
up and down this road here,

00:10:05.447 --> 00:10:08.760
70 and 80 miles an hour on a four-wheeler,

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.910
higher than a kite and
didn't even know it.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.580
He's buried right up there.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.720
They got the people that did it,

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.670
but every time I look
at that, to this day,

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:24.150
you know, I've forgot about a lot of it,

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:27.560
but to this day, it really gets to ya

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.760
seeing something like that.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:36.280
I've seen more deaths up and
down this highway right yonder.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.050
I've seen things you wouldn't believe

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:40.033
on that highway early of a morning.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:46.210
A skeleton crossing the
road, caskets going across,

00:10:46.986 --> 00:10:50.020
now, believe me, I'm telling
you the God's honest truth.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.970
Some of the things that I've
seen, you wouldn't believe me.

00:10:54.217 --> 00:10:55.380
That's the reason I kind of watch out

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.380
for Alyssa out through there of a night.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:03.193
'Cause I've seen, you don't never know.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.570
Little girl, her sleeping
in the room by herself.

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:10.370
You don't know who's
gonna be messing around.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.226
You'd be surprised, some
of the people I've caught

00:11:12.226 --> 00:11:14.240
right out there in that curve,

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.233
right behind Ella Mae's trailer,

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.100
and they didn't know I
was within a mile of 'em.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:20.780
Of a night, I get out and I walk around

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.096
'cause I can't hardly, where I smoke,

00:11:23.096 --> 00:11:25.013
I can't hardly breathe,

00:11:26.187 --> 00:11:27.893
and I'm about to lay that down.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:32.923
- [Mark] You have good friends?

00:11:32.923 --> 00:11:34.690
- Huh?
- You have friends?

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.620
- Very few anymore.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:39.760
But other than that, nah, I
don't deal with 'em, though.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.310
I don't hardly deal with nobody no more.

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:42.700
I keep right to myself.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.010
- [Mark] What about your family?

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.760
You see your mom, right?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:49.313
- I'm not too close with my
family, that's the truth.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.720
But now I've got a lot of friends

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.350
down the road, don't get me wrong.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:56.193
I'm distancing myself from my old friends,

00:11:57.274 --> 00:11:58.650
and I set myself on course

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.893
and I made myself a bunch of new friends.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.500
- [Mark] Are you happy?

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:07.910
- Yeah, I'm the happiest
I've been in a long time.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.050
I sit around and think about
the things I used to do

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:13.123
and I laugh, you wouldn't believe,

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.880
and some of the people I
meet, I get so tickled,

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.170
I swear, tears roll right down my eyes.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.900
I'm telling you the God's honest truth.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:24.970
- [Mark] Do you feel like you've lived

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.370
the life that you wanted to?

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:31.413
- Well, the way I see it, I've lived,

00:12:31.413 --> 00:12:33.610
I've lived and done about most things

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.450
that only most men around this area

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.003
could even dream about.

00:12:39.013 --> 00:12:42.887
The way I see it, have I
lived my life to the fullest?

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.713
No, I don't think I have yet.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.580
- [Mark] And you're happy living here?

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.550
- Not here, I'm not.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.380
- [Mark] But this part of the country?

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:58.210
- Yeah, this part of the county,

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.903
but I'm just not happy
in Curry Branch anymore.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:05.050
For one thing, there's too much damage.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.670
These homes have been
destroyed right here,

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:09.203
you can't get no help to do nothing.

00:13:09.203 --> 00:13:10.690
- [Mark] Yeah, a lot
of 'em are just shacks.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:11.523
- Huh?

00:13:11.523 --> 00:13:12.570
- [Mark] A lot of 'em
are just, they look like-

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:13.710
- They're just flat-out wiped out.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.260
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:18.390
- I spent over $3,200 right
there inside that trailer.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:19.543
Ran out of funds,

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:23.147
just lost it all.

00:13:24.874 --> 00:13:25.970
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.120
you've learned in life?

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.113
- Never trust nobody, except yourself.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.330
Always watch, always listen

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:37.743
and learn to who's talking around you,

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:43.210
and most of all, if a woman
goes out on you one time,

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.360
get rid of her the next day,

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:48.103
'cause she will do it agan every time.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:50.083
- [Mark] All right, Markum Ray,

00:13:50.083 --> 00:13:51.534
thank you so much of talking with me, man.

00:13:51.534 --> 00:13:52.900
- You're welcome.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.680
- [Mark] So glad we met.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.513
- Appreciate it.

00:13:55.513 --> 00:13:56.680
- [Mark] Thank you, man.

